  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Budget 2026: Healey hikes taxes on banks and landlords to fund £100 handouts to 20m households",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/28/budget-2026-healey-hikes-taxes-on-banks-and-landlords-to-fund-100-handouts-to-20m-households",
      "description": "<p>Few surprises as chancellor uses low-key speech blaming ‘global economic storms’ for stoking energy prices and cost of living crisis</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/28/budget-2026-key-points-john-healey\">Budget 2026: key points at a glance</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/money/2026/oct/28/budget-briefing-the-key-questions-answered-by-heather-stewart-and-pippa-crerar\">Briefing: key questions answered by Heather Stewart and Pippa Crerar</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/oct/28/the-guardian-view-on-labours-budget-bold-ambitions-and-welcome-first-steps\">Editorial: Budget’s bold ambitions and welcome first steps</a></p></li></ul><p>John Healey raised taxes on banks and landlords to fund a £100 winter handout for 20 million families as official forecasts made clear there is no end in sight for the cost of living crisis.</p><p>In his first budget, the chancellor blamed “global economic storms” for the grim outlook, as the war in Iran drives up oil and gas prices.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/28/budget-2026-healey-hikes-taxes-on-banks-and-landlords-to-fund-100-handouts-to-20m-households\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T20:09:34"
    },
    {
      "title": "Nigel Farage skips budget in Commons over seating ‘altercation’ concerns",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/28/nigel-farage-reform-uk-budget-commons-seating-row-ukraine-crypto",
      "description": "<p>Reform UK leader ‘shocked’ by £10bn pledged to Ukraine and doubles down on cutting tax for crypto investors</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/28/budget-2026-key-points-john-healey\">Budget 2026: key points at a glance</a></p></li></ul><p>Nigel Farage skipped <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/28/budget-2026-john-healey-offers-100-payment-to-households-to-help-navigate-global-economic-storms\">the chancellor’s first budget</a> because he was worried he would get in a “physical altercation” with another MP in a row over seating arrangements.</p><p>The Reform UK leader was not present in the House of Commons but gave a press conference afterwards in which he said he was “shocked” by the £10bn going to support Ukraine and doubled down on his party’s policies on cutting tax for crypto investors.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/28/nigel-farage-reform-uk-budget-commons-seating-row-ukraine-crypto\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T19:42:20"
    },
    {
      "title": "Budget 2026: £100 energy payment for millions and rise in bank tax as watchdog warns on stalling living standards – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2026/oct/28/budget-2026-latest-updates-john-healey-andy-burnham-labour-uk-politics",
      "description": "<p>OBR says that living standards are forecast to rise by just 1% over the whole post-Covid decade</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/28/budget-2026-key-points-john-healey\">Budget 2026: key points at a glance</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Martin Lewis</strong> <a href=\"https://x.com/MartinSLewis/status/2115360340720353765\">said</a> that, when he met John Healey this morning, the chancellor said that, having removed standing charges from gas bills, he would also like to get rid of them from electricity bills. Lewis said:</p><p>The chancellor said he will be talking to Ofgem about how they get rid of the charge on electricity as well, but that is ‘trickier’ apparently and will take longer.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2026/oct/28/budget-2026-latest-updates-john-healey-andy-burnham-labour-uk-politics\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T18:24:25"
    }
  ]
